WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.430
With so many moving parts and such high standards
to uphold, it's always possible that something

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.450
is going to go wrong on the set of Game of
Thrones.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:12.880
Throughout the show's eight seasons, a number
of performers have suffered for their art.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:13.880
Here's how.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.750
Sandor Clegane is so fearsome that the character
earned one of the coolest nicknames in all

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.029
of Game of Thrones: "The Hound."

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:25.329
He's survived trial by combat, a massacre
by the Freys, and being thrown off a cliff

00:00:25.329 --> 00:00:26.869
by Brienne of Tarth.

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:31.259
The actor who portrays Clegane, Rory McCann,
got a bit battered, too.

00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:33.090
"You want to cut my throat?

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.730
GET ON WITH IT!"

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:39.250
The seventh season episode "Beyond the Wall"
finds the Hound and others waging war against

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.020
the Night King and his forces.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:45.380
Clegane has to carry a wight through much
of the trek, forcing McCann to dash here and

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:50.100
there, sometimes across real ice, while the
actor playing the undead creature twisted

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.539
and tumbled on his shoulders.

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:55.730
It all left McCann with such intense pain
that he sat for an interview with the Sydney

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.039
Morning Herald while holding an ice pack to
his leg.

00:00:59.039 --> 00:01:00.039
McCann told the paper,

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:02.679
"I had this guy on my shoulder for days and
days.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:07.560
It didn't work with a dummy so I had to carry
a real guy and we had to run and run."

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:13.600
Jon Snow is the sensitive, brooding, and sometimes
pouty leading man of the Game of Thrones universe,

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.720
but you can't blame him for that, really,
because a lot of bad stuff has happened to

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.560
him.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.080
"For the watch!"

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:29.040
Playing Jon Snow has been much more pleasant
for actor Kit Harington.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.920
Game of Thrones brought him international
stardom, an Emmy nomination, and the hand

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.920
in marriage of co-star Rose Leslie.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.200
But also, quite nearly, permanent mutilation.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.470
Filming a dragon-flying scene for the show's
eighth season involved Harington mounting

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:45.830
a massive, flailing mechanical apparatus called
a "buck."

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:51.010
His character had to almost fall off, forcing
Harington to hold on… and to endure a tight

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.010
squeeze.

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:57.450
"And my right ball got trapped, and I didn't
have time to say 'Stop!'

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.740
And I was being swung around."

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:04.120
Fortunately, Harington finished the scene
and escaped with all of his parts intact.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.880
Since Season 2, actress Gemma Whelan has played
Yara Greyjoy, the now undisputed Queen of

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.430
the Iron Islands.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:15.180
She's a relentless warrior and commander of
a ship called the Black Wind, and a lot of

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.170
her scenes involve battles at sea.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:21.550
Whelan was filming a scene near Belfast, Northern
Ireland, for the seventh season of Game of

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:26.270
Thrones when she sustained some kind of injury
requiring hospitalization.

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:32.030
On September 14, 2016, Whelan posted to her
Instagram account a photo of some old-fashioned,

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.670
hospital-issue underwear.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:37.820
The pic came with a wry caption from Whelan,
describing how a ward nurse offered her the

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:42.810
undergarments because she arrived at the hospital,
quote, "a bit suddenly and unprepared."

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:47.490
Whelan never confirmed exactly what happened
to her on set or how, but she soon rejoined

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.080
the series.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:53.750
Eight seasons of Game of Thrones built up
to "The Long Night," the episode featuring

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:58.490
the Battle of Winterfell, the apocalyptic
confrontation between a massive army of zombie-like

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:02.740
White Walkers controlled by the Night King
and the assorted, united human contingents

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.910
of Westeros taking a break from fighting one
another.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:10.400
It's one of the largest sequences ever filmed
for Game of Thrones, which made for an intense,

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.510
grueling shoot.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.130
"We're fighting death!

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.490
I can't beat death."

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:20.480
In March 2019, Entertainment Weekly reported
that one of the series' regular actresses

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.810
suddenly collapsed on set while filming a
scene that involved what the outlet described

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.240
as "a lot of standing still."

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:31.180
A crew member noticed the fall right away
and called out for a medic, who promptly tended

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:32.860
to the unnamed actress.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.970
The official line: the actress fainted, went
home, and returned to the set the following

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:37.960
day.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.069
Part of what makes Game of Thrones so thrilling
is the scenery.

00:03:42.069 --> 00:03:46.430
The series has shot in exotic locations all
around the world, and filmed many sequences

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:51.150
in the breathtaking, rocky wilds of Northern
Ireland, which stood in nicely for the hinterlands

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:53.370
of the Seven Kingdoms and beyond.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:58.020
While it looks great on screen, the area posed
its own unique challenges for the production,

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.980
particularly the elements.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:04.290
The weather can get awfully brutal just off
the sea in the northern United Kingdom.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:09.180
While shooting near the village of Ballintoy
in 2011, the crew erected a pole tent where

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.690
workers and extras could have lunch.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:16.090
Then winds from Hurricane Katia whipped through
the area and tore the whole thing down, according

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.809
to the Belfast Telegraph.

00:04:17.809 --> 00:04:22.889
In the chaos, four men and one woman sustained
minor injuries, enough to briefly land them

00:04:22.889 --> 00:04:24.770
in the hospital.

